## Noncommercial Purposes
Any use of the software is allowed, except for commercial purposes:

1. A "commercial purpose" is any use of the software:
   a. As part of a business, commercial enterprise, hosting provider, or cloud reseller that charges fees or consideration for goods or services;
   b. As part of a paid commercial product, proprietary SaaS, or commercial application store listing;
   c. To generate revenue, directly or indirectly; or
   d. In exchange for payment, subscription, sponsorship, or monetary consideration of any kind.

2. A "noncommercial purpose" includes:
   a. Personal, non-monetized server and cloud infrastructure monitoring;
   b. Academic research, study, educational courses, and private experimentation;
   c. Security audits, code inspection, and bug bounty evaluation;
   d. Community contributions and pull requests back to the official upstream VaultScope repositories.

